<% content_for :title, "Demo 6: OAuth / API Connector" %>

<div class="container py-5">

  <%# Back to Home %>
  <div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col">
      <%= link_to root_path, class: "btn btn-outline-secondary" do %>
        <i class="bi bi-arrow-left me-1"></i> Back to Demo Selection
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Hero Section %>
  <div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-8 mx-auto text-center">
      <span class="badge mb-3 text-white" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">Demo 6</span>
      <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3">
        <i class="bi bi-plug me-2" style="color: #be123c;"></i>
        OAuth / API Connector
      </h1>
      <p class="lead text-muted">
        Connect any HTTP/REST API to your agent without writing code: point the connector at an
        OpenAPI spec and every endpoint becomes a tool, with OAuth2 authentication handled for you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# What is the OAuth/API connector %>
  <div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="card border-primary">
        <div class="card-header text-white" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">
          <h5 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-question-circle me-2"></i>
            What is the OAuth/API connector?
          </h5>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <p>
            The connector turns the endpoints of an existing HTTP/REST API into tools of your
            agent: one tool per endpoint. You never write code. You either describe the
            endpoints (<code>oauth_endpoints_json</code>) or, as in this demo, point it at an
            OpenAPI spec (<code>oauth_openapi_url</code>) and let it import them.
          </p>
          <ul class="mb-3">
            <li><strong>Authentication is handled for you:</strong> <code>none</code>,
              <code>bearer_static</code>, <code>oauth2_client_credentials</code>,
              <code>oauth2_password</code>, <code>oauth2_refresh</code>,
              <code>oauth2_jwt_bearer</code>. The token is cached and renewed automatically.
              This demo uses <code>oauth2_client_credentials</code> with a token that
              expires after 15 minutes, so you can watch the renewal happen.</li>
            <li><strong>Parameters travel where you want them:</strong> query string, path
              (<code>/commesse/{id}</code>) or JSON body. This API uses all three.</li>
            <li><strong>The agent does not memorise the tools.</strong> It asks the
              gateway for them. Update the API and the agent gets the new tools without
              being rebuilt. That also means the <code>summary</code> and
              <code>description</code> of each endpoint <em>are</em> part of the prompt:
              write them as instructions.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="alert alert-warning mb-0 small">
            <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle me-1"></i>
            Only <code>https://</code> URLs are accepted, and responses over ~40&nbsp;KB are
            truncated. That is why every list endpoint here is paginated and there is a
            <code>/kpi/riepilogo</code> endpoint for counting instead of downloading.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Where the gestionale comes from %>
  <div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="card border-primary">
        <div class="card-header text-white" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">
          <h5 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-building-gear me-2"></i>
            Where the gestionale comes from
          </h5>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <p>
            The other demos hand you a service that is already there. Here the API on the far
            side is one we built for the course. It is a small
            <strong>ERP</strong> ("gestionale"): six customers, a couple of dozen projects
            (<em>commesse</em>) with status, completion percentage, value and deadline, plus a
            progress log. In your company this is <strong>your own private management system</strong>
            (ERP, CRM, ticketing, whatever holds the data your colleagues ask about). Nothing
            in the connector setup changes: it never knows the difference.
          </p>

          <h6 class="fw-bold mt-4">How it was built</h6>
          <p class="text-muted small mb-2">
            Roughly 500 lines in <code>demo/docker/gestionale/</code>, five pieces:
          </p>
          <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-bordered table-sm">
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td class="fw-bold bg-light" style="width: 190px;"><code>db.py</code> + <code>seed.py</code></td>
                  <td>SQLite with three tables (<code>clienti</code>, <code>commesse</code>,
                    <code>avanzamenti</code>), filled with realistic sample data at startup. A real
                    gestionale has a real database here, so that part is already done for you.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="fw-bold bg-light"><code>main.py</code></td>
                  <td>FastAPI with four read endpoints, written <em>for an agent to use</em>: lists
                    are paginated and pre-sorted by urgency, and there is a
                    <code>/kpi/riepilogo</code> so the agent counts with one small call instead of
                    downloading every row.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="fw-bold bg-light"><code>POST /token</code></td>
                  <td>The OAuth2 <em>client credentials</em> endpoint. It checks the client
                    id/secret and returns a JWT that expires after 15 minutes. The connector calls
                    it on its own and renews the token, so you never handle it.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="fw-bold bg-light"><code>/openapi.json</code></td>
                  <td>Generated by FastAPI from the code itself, not written by hand.
                    <strong>This is the contract the connector imports:</strong> every operation in
                    it becomes a tool, and each one's <code>summary</code> and
                    <code>description</code> become the instructions the agent reads.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="fw-bold bg-light"><code>Dockerfile</code></td>
                  <td>python:3.12-slim running uvicorn on port 8100, started as the
                    <code>gestionale</code> service by the one-click starter below.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h6 class="fw-bold mt-4">How it gets out of your laptop</h6>
          <p>
            The API listens on <code>localhost:8100</code>, which AIsuru cannot reach, and the
            connector only accepts <code>https://</code> addresses. So the starter opens an
            <strong>ngrok</strong> tunnel and gives you a public HTTPS hostname pointing at your
            container. That is a demo device: <strong>in production your gestionale already has an
            HTTPS address</strong> reachable by AIsuru (or you expose a read-only slice of it behind
            your firewall), ngrok disappears, and every other value stays exactly the same.
          </p>

          <h6 class="fw-bold mt-4">To do this with your own API</h6>
          <ol class="mb-3">
            <li>It must be reachable over <strong>HTTPS</strong>.</li>
            <li>It needs an <strong>OpenAPI spec</strong>. Most frameworks generate one (FastAPI,
              NestJS, Spring, Rails with rswag). If yours does not, describe the endpoints by hand
              in <code>oauth_endpoints_json</code> instead.</li>
            <li>Its authentication must be one the connector speaks: static bearer token,
              OAuth2 client credentials, password, refresh, JWT bearer, or none at all.</li>
            <li>Write the <strong>summary and description of every endpoint as instructions for the
              agent</strong>, not as notes for developers. They end up in the prompt.</li>
          </ol>

          <div class="alert alert-info mb-0 small">
            <i class="bi bi-lightbulb me-1"></i>
            <strong>The point of all this:</strong> a colleague asks "how many projects are we late
            on for Rossi Spa this month?" and gets an answer in chat. No login to the
            gestionale, no export, and no MCP server written by you.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Setup Instructions %>
  <% unless @show_agent %>
    <%# Architecture Diagram %>
    <div class="row mb-4">
      <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f8f9fa 0%, #e9ecef 100%);">
          <div class="card-body text-center py-4">
            <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">Architecture</h6>
            <div class="d-flex justify-content-center align-items-center flex-wrap gap-2">
              <span class="badge bg-primary fs-6 px-3 py-2">AIsuru Agent</span>
              <i class="bi bi-arrow-right text-muted fs-4"></i>
              <span class="badge fs-6 px-3 py-2" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">OAuth/API Connector<br><small class="fw-normal">(MCP server, generated)</small></span>
              <i class="bi bi-arrow-right text-muted fs-4"></i>
              <span class="badge bg-dark fs-6 px-3 py-2">ngrok HTTPS</span>
              <i class="bi bi-arrow-right text-muted fs-4"></i>
              <span class="badge bg-success fs-6 px-3 py-2">FastAPI ERP (Docker)</span>
              <i class="bi bi-arrow-right text-muted fs-4"></i>
              <span class="badge bg-warning fs-6 px-3 py-2">SQLite</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# One-click starter %>
    <%= render "shared/infra_launcher", demo: "demo6", color: "linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%)" %>

    <%# Setup Instructions (manual fallback) %>
    <div class="row mb-4" id="manual-setup">
      <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <div class="card border-primary">
          <div class="card-header text-white" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">
            <h5 class="mb-0">
              <i class="bi bi-tools me-2"></i>
              Manual Setup Guide: OAuth / API Connector
            </h5>
          </div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <p class="text-muted mb-4">
              This is the step-by-step alternative to the one-click starter above. Use it if the button
              doesn't work or if you want to understand what happens under the hood.
              The agent will be able to query and update the ERP through its REST API.
            </p>

            <%# Step 1 %>
            <div class="d-flex mb-4">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
                <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">1</span>
              </div>
              <div class="flex-grow-1">
                <h6 class="fw-bold">Configure ngrok Authentication</h6>
                <p class="text-muted mb-2">
                  Get your ngrok auth token from <a href="https://dashboard.ngrok.com/get-started/your-authtoken" target="_blank">ngrok dashboard</a>.
                  Create a <code>.env</code> file in the demo directory:
                </p>
                <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded mb-1"><code>NGROK_AUTHTOKEN=your_token_here</code></pre>
              </div>
            </div>

            <%# Step 2 %>
            <div class="d-flex mb-4">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
                <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">2</span>
              </div>
              <div class="flex-grow-1">
                <h6 class="fw-bold">Free the ngrok Tunnel (if needed)</h6>
                <p class="text-muted mb-2">
                  <strong>⚠️ ngrok free accounts support only 1 active tunnel.</strong> If you were using another demo, stop all ngrok tunnels first:
                </p>
                <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded mb-1"><code>docker compose stop ngrok-mongo ngrok-mcp ngrok-demo2 ngrok-gestionale</code></pre>
                <small class="text-muted">
                  This stops all ngrok tunnels, freeing the connection for this demo.
                </small>
              </div>
            </div>

            <%# Step 3 %>
            <div class="d-flex mb-4">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
                <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">3</span>
              </div>
              <div class="flex-grow-1">
                <h6 class="fw-bold">Start the ERP and its Tunnel</h6>
                <p class="text-muted mb-2">
                  Start the fake ERP (FastAPI) and the ngrok tunnel that exposes it over HTTPS:
                </p>
                <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded mb-1"><code>docker compose up -d gestionale
docker compose up -d ngrok-gestionale</code></pre>
                <small class="text-muted">
                  Access the ngrok dashboard at <a href="http://localhost:4045" target="_blank" class="text-decoration-none">http://localhost:4045</a> to see the public HTTPS URL.
                </small>
              </div>
            </div>

            <%# Step 4 %>
            <div class="d-flex mb-3">
              <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
                <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">4</span>
              </div>
              <div class="flex-grow-1">
                <h6 class="fw-bold">Build the six connector values</h6>
                <p class="text-muted mb-2">
                  Take the tunnel's <strong>HTTPS URL</strong> (e.g. <code>https://abc123.ngrok-free.app</code>)
                  and build the six values you will paste into AIsuru in the next section:
                </p>
                <div class="table-responsive">
                  <table class="table table-bordered table-sm mb-2">
                    <tbody>
                      <tr>
                        <td class="fw-bold bg-light" style="width: 200px;"><code>oauth_auth_type</code></td>
                        <td><code>oauth2_client_credentials</code></td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td class="fw-bold bg-light"><code>oauth_token_url</code></td>
                        <td><code>https://<span class="text-danger">&lt;YOUR_NGROK_URL&gt;</span>/token</code></td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td class="fw-bold bg-light"><code>oauth_client_id</code></td>
                        <td><code>aisuru-demo</code></td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td class="fw-bold bg-light"><code>oauth_client_secret</code></td>
                        <td><code>demo-secret-sys06</code></td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td class="fw-bold bg-light"><code>oauth_scope</code></td>
                        <td><code>commesse:read</code></td>
                      </tr>
                      <tr>
                        <td class="fw-bold bg-light"><code>oauth_openapi_url</code></td>
                        <td><code>https://<span class="text-danger">&lt;YOUR_NGROK_URL&gt;</span>/openapi.json</code></td>
                      </tr>
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
                <small class="text-muted">
                  These credentials are printed here because this is a teaching demo. In
                  production they live in a secret store, which is what the connector does for you:
                  secrets are saved encrypted.
                </small>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# AIsuru side: required whichever route was taken above %>
    <%= render "shared/aisuru_mcp_setup", demo: "demo6", color: "linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%)" %>

    <%# Info about how to get Agent IDs %>
    <div class="row mb-4">
      <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
        <div class="card border-info">
          <div class="card-header bg-info text-white">
            <h5 class="mb-0">
              <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-2"></i>
              How to get your Agent IDs
            </h5>
          </div>
          <div class="card-body">
            <ol class="mb-0">
              <li class="mb-2">
                <strong>Create an Agent</strong> on <a href="https://www.aisuru.com" target="_blank">AIsuru</a>
                (or use your own tenant if you have a PaaS subscription)
              </li>
              <li class="mb-2">
                <strong>Open your Agent</strong> and click on <strong>"Dev docs"</strong> in the left sidebar
              </li>
              <li class="mb-2">
                Expand the <strong>"Other references"</strong> section (or "Altri riferimenti" in Italian)
              </li>
              <li class="mb-2">
                Copy the following values:
                <ul class="mt-2">
                  <li><strong>Secondary Memori (Agent) ID</strong> &rarr; This is your <code>memoriID</code></li>
                  <li><strong>Owner user ID</strong> &rarr; This is your <code>ownerUserID</code></li>
                </ul>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Configuration Form %>
    <div class="row mb-5">
      <div class="col-lg-8 mx-auto">
        <div class="card shadow">
          <div class="card-header text-white" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">
            <h5 class="mb-0">
              <i class="bi bi-gear me-2"></i>
              Configure Your Agent
            </h5>
          </div>
          <div class="card-body p-4">
            <%= form_with url: demo6_configure_path, method: :post, local: true do |f| %>
              <div class="mb-4">
                <label for="memori_id" class="form-label fw-bold">
                  <i class="bi bi-fingerprint me-1"></i>
                  Memori (Agent) Secondary ID *
                </label>
                <%= f.text_field :memori_id,
                    class: "form-control form-control-lg",
                    placeholder: "e.g., a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
                    required: true,
                    pattern: "[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}" %>
                <div class="form-text">
                  Found in Dev docs &rarr; Other references &rarr; "Secondary Memori (Agent) ID"
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="mb-4">
                <label for="owner_user_id" class="form-label fw-bold">
                  <i class="bi bi-person-badge me-1"></i>
                  Owner User ID
                </label>
                <%= f.text_field :owner_user_id,
                    class: "form-control form-control-lg",
                    placeholder: "e.g., b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-f12345678901",
                    required: true,
                    pattern: "[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}" %>
                <div class="form-text">
                  Found in Dev docs &rarr; Other references &rarr; "Owner user ID"
                </div>
              </div>

              <hr class="my-4">
              <h6 class="text-muted mb-3">
                <i class="bi bi-sliders me-1"></i>
                Advanced Configuration (pre-filled with defaults)
              </h6>

              <div class="row">
                <div class="col-md-6 mb-3">
                  <label for="tenant_id" class="form-label">
                    <i class="bi bi-building me-1"></i>
                    Tenant ID
                  </label>
                  <%= f.text_field :tenant_id,
                      class: "form-control",
                      value: @tenant_id || "www.aisuru.com",
                      required: true %>
                </div>

                <div class="col-md-6 mb-3">
                  <label for="base_url" class="form-label">
                    <i class="bi bi-link-45deg me-1"></i>
                    Base URL
                  </label>
                  <%= f.text_field :base_url,
                      class: "form-control",
                      value: @base_url || "https://www.aisuru.com",
                      required: true %>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="mb-3">
                <label for="engine_url" class="form-label">
                  <i class="bi bi-cpu me-1"></i>
                  Engine URL
                </label>
                <%= f.text_field :engine_url,
                    class: "form-control",
                    value: @engine_url || "https://engine.memori.ai/memori/v2",
                    required: true %>
              </div>

              <div class="mb-4">
                <label for="api_url" class="form-label">
                  <i class="bi bi-server me-1"></i>
                  API URL
                </label>
                <%= f.text_field :api_url,
                    class: "form-control",
                    value: @api_url || "https://backend.memori.ai/api/v2",
                    required: true %>
              </div>

              <div class="d-grid">
                <%= f.submit "Load Agent", class: "btn btn-lg text-white", style: "background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);" %>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <%# Agent & Live ERP Split View %>
  <% if @show_agent %>
    <%# Agent Info Banner %>
    <div class="row mb-3">
      <div class="col-12">
        <div class="alert d-flex align-items-center mb-0 text-white" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">
          <i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill me-2 fs-5"></i>
          <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <strong>Agent Connected!</strong>
            Chat with the agent on the left. It can query the ERP through its REST API.
            Click <strong>"Refresh"</strong> on the right to see live changes.
          </div>
          <%= link_to demo6_path, class: "btn btn-outline-light btn-sm ms-3" do %>
            <i class="bi bi-arrow-counterclockwise me-1"></i> Reconfigure
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Two-Column Layout %>
    <div class="row g-3">

      <%# LEFT: Agent %>
      <div class="col-lg-6">
        <div class="card shadow">
          <div class="card-header text-white d-flex align-items-center" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">
            <i class="bi bi-robot me-2"></i>
            <strong>AIsuru Agent</strong>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark ms-auto">API-enabled</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card-body p-0">
            <div class="memori-container" style="height: 650px;">
              <memori-client
                memoriName="YourAgent"
                ownerUserName="owner"
                memoriID="<%= @memori_id %>"
                ownerUserID="<%= @owner_user_id %>"
                tenantID="<%= @tenant_id %>"
                engineURL="<%= @engine_url %>"
                apiURL="<%= @api_url %>"
                baseURL="<%= @base_url %>"
                layout="CHAT"
                uiLang="EN"
                spokenLang="EN"
                showLogin="true"
              ></memori-client>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card shadow-sm mt-3">
          <div class="card-body py-3">
            <h6 class="text-muted mb-2">
              <i class="bi bi-chat-quote me-1"></i> Try these in the chat
            </h6>
            <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-2">
              <% [
                   "Quante commesse attive abbiamo questo mese?",
                   "Mostrami le commesse del cliente Rossi Spa che sono in ritardo",
                   "Porta la commessa CM-#{Date.current.year}-003 all'80% e annota: collaudo completato"
                 ].each do |prompt| %>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary text-start demo6-prompt"
                        data-prompt="<%= prompt %>">
                  <i class="bi bi-clipboard me-1"></i><%= prompt %>
                </button>
              <% end %>
            </div>
            <small class="text-muted d-block mt-2">
              Click to copy, then paste into the chat. The third one writes: watch the panel
              on the right change.
            </small>
            <small class="text-muted d-block mt-2">
              <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle me-1"></i>
              If the ERP container has been running for a while, "this month" and "in ritardo"
              may look stale. Use the <strong>Reset</strong> button on the right (or
              <code>docker compose down -v</code>) to regenerate fresh seed dates.
            </small>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# RIGHT: Live ERP data %>
      <div class="col-lg-6">
        <div class="card shadow h-100">
          <div class="card-header text-white d-flex align-items-center" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #be123c 0%, #fb7185 100%);">
            <i class="bi bi-kanban me-2"></i>
            <strong>Live ERP data</strong>
            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark ms-2">via REST API</span>
            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light ms-auto" onclick="refreshDashboard()">
              <i class="bi bi-arrow-clockwise me-1"></i> Refresh
            </button>
            <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light ms-2" onclick="resetDemoData()">
              <i class="bi bi-arrow-counterclockwise me-1"></i> Reset
            </button>
          </div>
          <div class="card-body" style="height: 650px; overflow-y: auto;">
            <div id="demo6-dashboard">
              <%= render partial: "demo6/dashboard" %>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <script>
      function refreshDashboard() {
        fetch('<%= demo6_commesse_path %>')
          .then(response => response.text())
          .then(html => {
            document.getElementById('demo6-dashboard').innerHTML = html;
          });
      }

      function resetDemoData() {
        fetch('<%= demo6_reset_path %>', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: {
            'X-CSRF-Token': document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]')?.content || '',
          },
        })
          .then(response => response.text())
          .then(html => {
            document.getElementById('demo6-dashboard').innerHTML = html;
          });
      }

      document.querySelectorAll('.demo6-prompt').forEach((btn) => {
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          navigator.clipboard.writeText(btn.dataset.prompt);
          const icon = btn.querySelector('i');
          icon.className = 'bi bi-check2 me-1';
          setTimeout(() => { icon.className = 'bi bi-clipboard me-1'; }, 1500);
        });
      });

      // Auto-refresh every 5 seconds
      setInterval(refreshDashboard, 5000);
    </script>
  <% end %>

</div>
